  {
   "id": "do-now-ext",
   "label": "Extension: Do Now Challenge",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y11-1-8-shifts",
   "embedContainerId": "y11-19d-do-now-ext",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Extension: Do Now Challenge</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does each card use new numbers?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Then you practise the method, not one answer.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\"><strong>Extension:</strong> finished the Do Now? Try these logical shift cards from 1.8. Stuck? Switch on <strong>I need help</strong>.</p><div id=\"y11-19d-do-now-ext\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "how-to-play",
   "label": "How to Play",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Circuit Siege: How to Play</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does the exam give a mark for the working?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It shows the examiner your method, so you can still earn a mark after a small slip.</p></div></details><ol class=\"lesson-facts\" style=\"font-size:22px;line-height:1.6\"><li>Answer two's complement exam questions to earn coins for your towers.</li><li>Type your <strong>working</strong> and your <strong>answer</strong> in the box, like in the exam.</li><li>Not full marks? Read the help, then try once more. A second try earns half.</li></ol>"
  },
  {
   "id": "game",
   "label": "Play: Circuit Siege",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "tower-defence",
   "embedQuery": "set=twos-complement",
   "embedContainerId": "y11-19d-game",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Play: Circuit Siege</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why check an answer by working backwards?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>If it does not give the number you started with, you know there is a slip to find.</p></div></details><div id=\"y11-19d-game\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "plenary",
   "label": "Plenary: Two's Complement Drill",
   "type": "embedded-app",
   "appId": "drill-y11-1-9-twos",
   "embedContainerId": "y11-19d-plenary",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Two's Complement Drill</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why practise with new numbers every time?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Then you know the method, not just one answer.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Read two's complement, make negative numbers and positive numbers. Your progress is saved.</p><div id=\"y11-19d-plenary\"></div>"
  }
